## Stack: <%= language %><% if (language === 'typescript') { %>

**Test runner:** vitest

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect } from "vitest";

describe("feature", () => {
  it("does the expected thing", () => {
    // Arrange
    // Act
    // Assert
    expect(result).toBe(expected);
  });
});
```
<% } else if (language === 'java') { %>

**Test runner:** JUnit 5 + Mockito

```java
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class FeatureTest {

    @Mock
    private Dependency dependency;

    @InjectMocks
    private Feature feature;

    @Test
    void shouldDoExpectedThing() {
        // Arrange
        when(dependency.call()).thenReturn(value);

        // Act
        var result = feature.execute();

        // Assert
        assertThat(result).isEqualTo(expected);
    }
}
```
<% } else if (language === 'python') { %>

**Test runner:** pytest

```python
def test_does_expected_thing():
    # Arrange
    # Act
    result = feature()

    # Assert
    assert result == expected
```
<% } else if (language === 'go') { %>

**Test runner:** Go standard `testing` package

```go
func TestFeature(t *testing.T) {
    // Arrange
    // Act
    got := Feature()

    // Assert
    if got != want {
        t.Errorf("Feature() = %v, want %v", got, want)
    }
}
```
<% } else if (language === 'rust') { %>

**Test runner:** Rust built-in `#[test]` + `#[cfg(test)]`

```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn test_does_expected_thing() {
        // Arrange
        // Act
        let result = feature();

        // Assert
        assert_eq!(result, expected);
    }
}
```
<% } %>

## Rules

- One behavior per test
- Watch each test fail before implementing
- Minimal code to pass — no extra features
- Refactor only after green

## When to Skip TDD

Only with explicit user permission. "This is simple" is never a reason.
